## --- AsyncFile -----------------------------------------------------
##
## Owning wrapper around a non-blocking POSIX fd. Wire-compatible with
## RivenFile (8 bytes: int32 fd + int32 closed). Drop closes the fd —
## the C side's `riven_async_file_drop` is idempotent.
##
## `fd` and `closed` are field-level Ints in Riven but the C struct
## (RivenAsyncFile in runtime/async_fs.c) lays them out as int32s. The
## codegen for class fields packs sub-i64 fields by their declared
## type — but here Int is i64 in Riven, which would put us at 16 bytes
## not 8. This is OK in v1 because the wire layout is owned by the C
## allocator (`riven_async_file_open` returns a freshly-allocated
## 8-byte struct), and the Riven class never directly allocates: it
## only borrows existing pointers from C. The fields here are
## declared for the `def drop` body to consult, but in practice the
## drop body delegates to the C-side `riven_async_file_drop` which
## reads the i32 layout directly.
##
## TODO when v1.1 tightens layout: add a `repr(C, 8-byte)` annotation
## that pins Riven-side field sizes to the C wire format.
class AsyncFile
  fd: Int
  closed: Int

  ## Construct an AsyncOpenFuture for read-only access. Returns the
  ## future eagerly — its first poll completes the open(2) synchronously
  ## (regular files are non-blocking even without O_NONBLOCK; the
  ## O_NONBLOCK flag is still set so subsequent read futures can park
  ## on EAGAIN if the fd is a pipe/fifo).
  def self.open(path: &String) -> AsyncOpenFuture
    AsyncOpenFuture.new(path, 0)
  end

  ## Construct an AsyncOpenFuture for write+create+truncate access.
  ## Equivalent to sync `File.create(path)` plus O_NONBLOCK.
  def self.create(path: &String) -> AsyncOpenFuture
    AsyncOpenFuture.new(path, 1)
  end

  ## Construct an AsyncReadToStringFuture for this file. The future
  ## borrows the fd; the AsyncFile remains owner of the fd lifecycle
  ## (its `def drop` closes the fd). The future deregisters its own
  ## reactor registration on drop.
  def var read_to_string -> AsyncReadToStringFuture
    AsyncReadToStringFuture.new(riven_async_file_fd(self))
  end

  ## Construct an AsyncWriteAllFuture for this file with `content`.
  def var write_all(content: &String) -> AsyncWriteAllFuture
    AsyncWriteAllFuture.new(riven_async_file_fd(self), content)
  end

  ## C-side drop hook (closes the fd). Registered in user_drop_classes
  ## because this method exists; the MIR drop elaborator emits a call
  ## to `AsyncFile_drop` at scope exit followed by riven_dealloc.
  lib "runtime/async_fs.c"
    def drop as "riven_async_file_drop"(self) -> ()
  end
end

## AsyncFile-typed C decls. Live in a module-scope lib block AFTER
## the AsyncFile class so the return / param types resolve. Declared
## as free fns (not class methods) because they're called directly by
## the future state-machine bodies, not dispatched through `self`.
lib "runtime/async_fs.c"
  def riven_async_file_open(path: &String, flags: Int) -> Result[AsyncFile, IoError]
  def riven_async_file_fd(file: &AsyncFile) -> Int
end
